  "description": "Demolition of existing garage and front porch and the construction of a single storey front extension, a two storey side extension, a part two storey part single storey rear extension, and a rear dormer extension including two roof lights to the front to facilitate conversion of roof space into habitable accommodation",
  "development_type": "Other house holder developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of its design, bulk, mass, scale and siting, would appear incongruous and out of keeping with the prevailing character of the host dwelling and semi-detached pair and the distinctiveness and historic character of the Becontree Estate. The proposal would result in a detrimental loss of symmetry of the existing pair of dwellings and a&nbsp;loss of the open aspect to the corner plot. It would thereby cause undue harm to the character and appearance of the area, including&nbsp;moderate&nbsp;harm to the non-designated heritage asset. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character and historic distinctiveness:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policy HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021) The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012) Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4&nbsp;and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
